1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,902
Rockstar hides things in every GTA, and GTA

2
00:00:02,902 --> 00:00:05,804
6 is already full of them. Callbacks to

3
00:00:05,804 --> 00:00:08,706
Vice City, links to Liberty City and Red

4
00:00:08,706 --> 00:00:11,608
Dead, and one easter egg that is, quite

5
00:00:11,608 --> 00:00:12,696
literally, an egg.

6
00:00:12,946 --> 00:00:15,502
I'll be clear about what's confirmed and what's

7
00:00:15,502 --> 00:00:18,057
a fan theory, because a lot of what's

8
00:00:18,057 --> 00:00:20,613
going around online is guesswork. Let's start with

9
00:00:20,613 --> 00:00:22,210
the one everyone's talking about.

10
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:25,314
Players found a bird's nest full of colourful

11
00:00:25,314 --> 00:00:28,167
eggs at the top of a tower in

12
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:31,021
Leonida, reportedly a radio or communications tower. The

13
00:00:31,021 --> 00:00:32,804
climb takes about seven minutes.

14
00:00:33,054 --> 00:00:35,331
Take one of the eggs and throw it

15
00:00:35,331 --> 00:00:37,607
toward the ground, and a short cutscene plays

16
00:00:37,607 --> 00:00:39,884
showing the egg smashing onto the windscreen of

17
00:00:39,884 --> 00:00:41,022
a car driving below.

18
00:00:41,272 --> 00:00:44,107
The footage was shared on X by a

19
00:00:44,107 --> 00:00:46,942
player called xGarbett on November 18th, right after

20
00:00:46,942 --> 00:00:49,777
the game's staggered release. You can even talk

21
00:00:49,777 --> 00:00:52,612
to an influencer at the top of the

22
00:00:52,612 --> 00:00:55,447
tower. The exact tower isn't confirmed in Rockstar's

23
00:00:55,447 --> 00:00:57,928
materials, so treat the location as player-reported.

24
00:00:58,178 --> 00:01:00,783
It's a nod to a classic: the original

25
00:01:00,783 --> 00:01:03,388
Vice City had a hidden room with an

26
00:01:03,388 --> 00:01:05,992
actual chocolate easter egg inside. Rockstar has been

27
00:01:05,992 --> 00:01:07,946
doing this for over twenty years.

28
00:01:08,196 --> 00:01:11,177
Tommy Vercetti isn't in GTA 6, but his

29
00:01:11,177 --> 00:01:14,159
name is. Two revolvers in the Ultimate Edition,

30
00:01:14,159 --> 00:01:17,140
the Hawk and the Little Morgan, are listed

31
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:20,121
as sourced from the Vercetti Estate, with palm-tree

32
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:21,612
engravings on the grips.

33
00:01:21,862 --> 00:01:25,057
And promo material shows Jason and Lucia outside

34
00:01:25,057 --> 00:01:28,253
the Ocean View Hotel, which was Tommy's very

35
00:01:28,253 --> 00:01:31,448
first safehouse in the 2002 game. That one

36
00:01:31,448 --> 00:01:33,046
is a deliberate callback.

37
00:01:33,296 --> 00:01:36,464
Fan theory territory: in the second trailer, a

38
00:01:36,464 --> 00:01:39,632
painting of an iguana appears to be wearing

39
00:01:39,632 --> 00:01:42,800
Tommy's famous tropical shirt. Fans spotted it, but

40
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,384
Rockstar hasn't confirmed it.

41
00:01:44,634 --> 00:01:47,505
Why does this matter? Because it confirms that

42
00:01:47,505 --> 00:01:50,376
Vice City's history still exists in this universe.

43
00:01:50,376 --> 00:01:53,247
Tommy built an empire here, and decades later

44
00:01:53,247 --> 00:01:56,117
his estate is selling off guns. That's a

45
00:01:56,117 --> 00:01:58,988
great bit of world-building for anyone who played

46
00:01:58,988 --> 00:01:59,706
the original.

47
00:01:59,956 --> 00:02:03,018
Flash FM is back. It was a radio

48
00:02:03,018 --> 00:02:06,081
station in the original Vice City, and Rockstar

49
00:02:06,081 --> 00:02:07,612
has confirmed its return.

50
00:02:07,862 --> 00:02:10,878
Slayer's Raining Blood is back too. It played

51
00:02:10,878 --> 00:02:13,895
on V-Rock in the original Vice City, and

52
00:02:13,895 --> 00:02:16,911
in GTA 6 it shows up on The

53
00:02:16,911 --> 00:02:19,928
Chamber 106.6, a station hosted by Slayer members

54
00:02:19,928 --> 00:02:22,190
as DJ Tom and DJ Kerry.

55
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:25,375
And Phil Collins' Against All Odds appears in

56
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:28,310
the extended promo footage. Collins was in Vice

57
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:31,245
City Stories, where he played a virtual concert

58
00:02:31,245 --> 00:02:32,712
at Hyman Memorial Stadium.

59
00:02:32,962 --> 00:02:35,852
In the second trailer, a man fires a

60
00:02:35,852 --> 00:02:38,742
weapon under a sign that reads Phil's Ammu-Nation.

61
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:41,632
Some fans think it's Phil Cassidy from Vice

62
00:02:41,632 --> 00:02:44,522
City, or a relative. Again, Rockstar hasn't confirmed

63
00:02:44,522 --> 00:02:46,690
it, so file this under theory.

64
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:49,479
If you never played the original: Phil Cassidy

65
00:02:49,479 --> 00:02:52,017
was Vice City's one-armed arms dealer, who ran

66
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:54,556
his own gun range out in the country.

67
00:02:54,556 --> 00:02:57,095
A Phil's Ammu-Nation is exactly the kind of

68
00:02:57,095 --> 00:02:59,633
joke Rockstar loves, which is why fans want

69
00:02:59,633 --> 00:03:01,220
this one to be real.

70
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:04,350
Here's a confirmed one from the official character

71
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:07,230
profiles. Lucia's mother wanted a good life for

72
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:10,110
her ever since their days in Liberty City,

73
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:12,990
the setting of GTA 3 and GTA 4.

74
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:16,016
And players have found books in the game

75
00:03:16,016 --> 00:03:18,792
that mention Red Dead Redemption and GTA 4.

76
00:03:18,792 --> 00:03:21,568
Rockstar keeps hinting that its worlds are connected.

77
00:03:21,818 --> 00:03:24,463
Another Red Dead link, this one a theory:

78
00:03:24,463 --> 00:03:27,108
during a TV scene with Jason, there's footage

79
00:03:27,108 --> 00:03:29,752
of animals grazing by a river just before

80
00:03:29,752 --> 00:03:32,397
a Prairie Sandwich Meal ad. Reddit users think

81
00:03:32,397 --> 00:03:35,042
that landscape comes from Red Dead Redemption 2.

82
00:03:35,292 --> 00:03:38,188
And a sticker in the first trailer appears

83
00:03:38,188 --> 00:03:41,084
to show Everett Morgan, a Red Dead Online

84
00:03:41,084 --> 00:03:43,980
character. Also unconfirmed, but it fits the pattern.

85
00:03:44,230 --> 00:03:47,073
Going back even further, the launch trailer shows

86
00:03:47,073 --> 00:03:49,916
North Fort Law. Longtime fans will recognise it

87
00:03:49,916 --> 00:03:52,759
as the military base from the very first

88
00:03:52,759 --> 00:03:55,246
GTA, in the State of New Guernsey.

89
00:03:55,496 --> 00:03:58,105
The trailer also leaves an open question there:

90
00:03:58,105 --> 00:04:00,714
we don't know if that's a flashback to

91
00:04:00,714 --> 00:04:03,324
Jason's army days or a present-day mission where

92
00:04:03,324 --> 00:04:05,933
he calls in old squadmates. TechWiser flagged it,

93
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:08,216
and nobody can say for sure yet.

94
00:04:08,466 --> 00:04:11,647
The classic brands are back. Weazel News appears

95
00:04:11,647 --> 00:04:14,828
to report on a police chase in the

96
00:04:14,828 --> 00:04:18,008
first trailer. Sessanta Nove, the fake luxury fashion

97
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:20,394
label from GTA 5, returns too.

98
00:04:20,644 --> 00:04:23,466
And here's one that escaped the game entirely:

99
00:04:23,466 --> 00:04:26,289
fans spotted real-life Weazel News ads in Miami.

100
00:04:26,289 --> 00:04:29,111
Rockstar's fake news network showed up in the

101
00:04:29,111 --> 00:04:31,228
real city that inspired Vice City.

102
00:04:31,478 --> 00:04:34,243
In extended footage, there's a Fleeca Bank sticker

103
00:04:34,243 --> 00:04:37,008
on Jason's fridge. And the launch trailer has

104
00:04:37,008 --> 00:04:39,772
a fried chicken bucket parody that fans linked

105
00:04:39,772 --> 00:04:41,846
to a well-known fast food chain.

106
00:04:42,096 --> 00:04:44,829
Fleeca, if you don't remember, was the bank

107
00:04:44,829 --> 00:04:47,563
chain from GTA 5, the one behind the

108
00:04:47,563 --> 00:04:50,296
Fleeca Job heist. Seeing it on Jason's fridge

109
00:04:50,296 --> 00:04:53,030
is a quiet way of saying Los Santos

110
00:04:53,030 --> 00:04:55,080
and Leonida share the same world.

111
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:58,306
And the '95 Grotti Cheetah is a modern

112
00:04:58,306 --> 00:05:01,282
take on the classic Cheetah sports car, with

113
00:05:01,282 --> 00:05:04,258
a retro-futuristic livery. It's one of the Ultimate

114
00:05:04,258 --> 00:05:05,002
Edition cars.

115
00:05:05,252 --> 00:05:08,561
Car fans also spotted a supercar in the

116
00:05:08,561 --> 00:05:11,870
launch trailer with a Ferrari SF90-style shape. Rockstar

117
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:15,178
always parodies real cars, and GTA 6 has

118
00:05:15,178 --> 00:05:17,660
some of its closest lookalikes yet.

119
00:05:17,910 --> 00:05:20,676
And honestly, the parodies are half the fun.

120
00:05:20,676 --> 00:05:23,442
Rockstar's sense of humour is sharpest when it's

121
00:05:23,442 --> 00:05:26,209
poking at real brands, and Leonida is clearly

122
00:05:26,209 --> 00:05:27,246
packed with them.

123
00:05:27,496 --> 00:05:30,053
Now the small stuff that makes Leonida feel

124
00:05:30,053 --> 00:05:32,611
alive. Weapons stay visible on your character even

125
00:05:32,611 --> 00:05:35,168
when you're sitting in a car as a

126
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:35,488
passenger.

127
00:05:35,738 --> 00:05:39,252
Firearms have serial numbers, and some of them

128
00:05:39,252 --> 00:05:42,765
reference previous GTA games. Rockstar hid easter eggs

129
00:05:42,765 --> 00:05:44,522
inside the guns themselves.

130
00:05:44,772 --> 00:05:47,851
The launch trailer also shows rideable electric scooters,

131
00:05:47,851 --> 00:05:50,931
multiple jet skis, and what looks like a

132
00:05:50,931 --> 00:05:54,010
returning blimp. Fans are hoping that blimp is

133
00:05:54,010 --> 00:05:54,780
flyable again.

134
00:05:55,030 --> 00:05:57,742
TechWiser spotted a Komodo dragon hiding in a

135
00:05:57,742 --> 00:06:00,454
swamp scene in the trailer, and a Marauder

136
00:06:00,454 --> 00:06:03,166
print on a shirt that matches an arm

137
00:06:03,166 --> 00:06:05,878
tattoo, possibly a hint at Jason's army past.

138
00:06:06,128 --> 00:06:09,046
And the six-star wanted level is back for

139
00:06:09,046 --> 00:06:11,965
the first time since GTA 4. GTA 5

140
00:06:11,965 --> 00:06:13,424
capped it at five.

141
00:06:13,674 --> 00:06:16,306
Six stars was last seen in GTA 4

142
00:06:16,306 --> 00:06:18,939
and Chinatown Wars, so bringing it back is

143
00:06:18,939 --> 00:06:21,571
a callback in itself, and a warning about

144
00:06:21,571 --> 00:06:23,874
how serious the police are this time.

145
00:06:24,124 --> 00:06:27,803
Even the wildlife has secrets. The in-game wildlife

146
00:06:27,803 --> 00:06:31,482
chart lists alligators, boars, bobcats, snakes and more,

147
00:06:31,482 --> 00:06:35,161
and it has a separate symbol for toxic

148
00:06:35,161 --> 00:06:38,380
waste. Somewhere in Leonida, something is glowing.

149
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:41,594
Flamingos and alligators share the Grassrivers, and the

150
00:06:41,594 --> 00:06:44,559
underwater areas hold treasure and secrets of their

151
00:06:44,559 --> 00:06:47,523
own. If a place looks empty, it usually

152
00:06:47,523 --> 00:06:47,894
isn't.

153
00:06:48,144 --> 00:06:50,746
There are secrets in Jason's own house, too.

154
00:06:50,746 --> 00:06:53,348
Under the loose floorboards in his bedroom, where

155
00:06:53,348 --> 00:06:55,950
you can stash cash, you'll find old photos

156
00:06:55,950 --> 00:06:57,576
that add to his backstory.

157
00:06:57,826 --> 00:07:00,429
And meet Dolores, Jason's pet snake. Feed her

158
00:07:00,429 --> 00:07:03,033
and you get a small early Focus boost.

159
00:07:03,033 --> 00:07:05,636
It's a tiny detail, but it tells you

160
00:07:05,636 --> 00:07:08,239
how much Rockstar wanted this world to feel

161
00:07:08,239 --> 00:07:08,890
lived in.

162
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:11,745
Gloriana is another fun one. People speculated it

163
00:07:11,745 --> 00:07:14,349
was a whole new state, but it appears

164
00:07:14,349 --> 00:07:16,628
to be just a single key island.

165
00:07:16,878 --> 00:07:19,969
Want to find your own? Use Focus Mode.

166
00:07:19,969 --> 00:07:23,060
It highlights interactables in yellow, so hidden notes

167
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:24,606
and objects stand out.

168
00:07:24,856 --> 00:07:27,798
Check the minimap inside shops for back rooms

169
00:07:27,798 --> 00:07:30,740
and staircases, and look for dark blue buildings

170
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:33,682
on the map, because those have interiors. Most

171
00:07:33,682 --> 00:07:36,256
secrets are inside, not on the street.

172
00:07:36,506 --> 00:07:39,202
And climb things. The egg was at the

173
00:07:39,202 --> 00:07:41,898
top of a seven-minute climb. If Rockstar put

174
00:07:41,898 --> 00:07:44,594
a long climb somewhere, there's usually a reason.

175
00:07:44,844 --> 00:07:47,717
And remember the scale here: more than seven

176
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:50,590
hundred enterable interiors have been reported. Rockstar hid

177
00:07:50,590 --> 00:07:53,463
that egg in one tower. Imagine what's sitting

178
00:07:53,463 --> 00:07:54,540
in the rest.

179
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:57,447
The fun part is that the community is

180
00:07:57,447 --> 00:08:00,104
still early. The game only came out days

181
00:08:00,104 --> 00:08:02,761
ago, so the biggest secrets almost certainly haven't

182
00:08:02,761 --> 00:08:05,086
been found yet. Expect a part two.

183
00:08:05,336 --> 00:08:08,117
And if Rockstar's history is any guide, some

184
00:08:08,117 --> 00:08:10,898
of the best ones will take months or

185
00:08:10,898 --> 00:08:13,679
even years to surface. People were still finding

186
00:08:13,679 --> 00:08:16,112
new Vice City secrets long after 2002.

187
00:08:16,362 --> 00:08:19,655
Quick recap of the confirmed ones: the tower

188
00:08:19,655 --> 00:08:22,948
egg, the Vercetti Estate revolvers, the Ocean View

189
00:08:22,948 --> 00:08:26,241
Hotel, Flash FM, Raining Blood on The Chamber,

190
00:08:26,241 --> 00:08:29,534
Lucia's Liberty City past, and the six-star wanted

191
00:08:29,534 --> 00:08:29,946
level.

192
00:08:30,196 --> 00:08:32,622
What's the best easter egg you've found? Drop

193
00:08:32,622 --> 00:08:35,048
it in the comments with where you found

194
00:08:35,048 --> 00:08:37,475
it, and I might feature it in the

195
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:39,901
next video. And subscribe for more GTA 6

196
00:08:39,901 --> 00:08:40,204
secrets.
